{title: Once in Royal David's City}
{artist: Cecil Frances Alexander & Henry Gauntlett}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 84}

Verse 1
[F]Once in royal [C]David's [F]city [Bb]stood a [F]lowly [C]cattle [F]shed,
where a mother [C]laid her [F]baby [Bb]in a [F]manger [C]for his [F]bed:
[Bb]Mary was that [F]mother mild, [Bb]Jesus [F]Christ her [C]little [F]child.
